CORE
main.c
--unwind 3 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --verbosity 9
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
 variables, 
--
^[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]* variables,
--
The disallowed pattern is the point of this test: it matches a variable count
of seven digits or more. A 10000-element array handled by the array decision
procedure must not cost one SAT variable per bit. Before the fix this program
encoded to 4487727 variables, after it to 7727, for the same 20495 clauses and
the same verdict -- the removed variables never appeared in a clause.

Note test.pl matches with grep, so these are basic regular expressions: no
'+' or '{n,m}' quantifiers, hence the spelled-out digit runs.
